{"parentUuid":"03f140d7-869e-499f-9ba1-6b92c698c45b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01FSLjpPHeccEQW6rnyWbaST","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0a64cf71-15a8-41de-8c8a-b821373f3bb7","timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:04:53.860Z","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"fix/release-pr-stage-only","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"0a64cf71-15a8-41de-8c8a-b821373f3bb7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMu65ZhVyMcCUocCGcjL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #359 is open: https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/359. It fixes two release-note and changelog bugs, and `just ci` passed locally.\n\n- **Notes cut short:** a `# ` or `## ` line inside a code block, or indented under a list item, ended the section early. A section now ends only at an unindented heading outside a code block.\n- **Duplicate title:** a changelog that starts with a byte order mark gained a second title. It now keeps the mark and a single title.\n- **Siblings:** `find_section` is the only copy of that logic, so nothing else needed the same fix.\n\nThe branch name is `fix/release-pr-stage-only` because I created it for the `git add -A` item, which I dropped. The #353 path allow-list already rejects stray files in a release commit.\n\nFirst-run setup on a mixed Cargo, npm and PyPI repo works end to end (`init`, `add`, `status`, `release --dry-run`). A repo with no root manifest at all fails at the first command with E030. The error says what to add, so I left it. Making `init` handle that case is a design choice for you.\n\nRelease PR #349 should refresh itself now that the merges landed. I haven't confirmed that yet.\n\nRemaining queue is small: the E121 message for an uncommitted first run, snapshot `--tag` validation, Poetry comment loss, Python `~=` precision, and the first-release metadata preflight. I'm taking the first-release preflight next, since it's the likeliest to hit a new user's first publish.\n\nresult: PR #359 opened to stop release notes being cut short by code blocks and to fix duplicate titles in changelogs with a byte order mark, with full local CI passing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":515,"cache_read_i