record | Put the Python package in its own d\n| E008 | Package identity has an ecosystem prefix but no name after it | Include package name after ecosystem prefix. |\n| E009 | Manifest path has an unsupported format | — |\n| E010 | Failed to read a manifest file | Check file permissions and path validity. |\n| E011 | Failed to write a manifest file | Check write permissions on target directory. |\n| E012 | Manifest is not valid for its declared format | Verify manifest syntax formatting. |\n| E013 | Manifest is missing a required field | Add a `<field>` field to the manifest, or exclude it from workspace discovery. |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0392327b-b45e-4f37-8364-11cb5cdcdbac","timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:37:33.620Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs:423:        if let Some(pub_val) = p.get(\"publish\") {\ncrates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs:340:        \"package `{package}` configures publish-to target `{target}` (ecosystem `{}`), but its detected ecosystem is `{}`\",\ncrates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs:346:        help(\"Remove the mismatched target from publish-to, or fix the [[package]]/[[package-set]] rule so it only matches packages in that ecosystem.\")\ncrates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs:744:    #[error(\"package `{package}` configures publish-to = [\\\"{target}\\\"], which release cannot dispatch yet\")]\ncrates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs:747:        help(\"Remove the target from `publish-to` for this package, or publish it outside `callisto release`.\")\ncrates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs:1125:    #[error(\"`publish-to` names registry key `{key}`, which no [registries.*] block defines\")]\ncrates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs:1229:                    args: vec![\"publish\".to_owned()],\ncrates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs:686:        // Apply the resolved override's publish-to if the operator explicitly set it.\ncrates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs:694:        // `publish-to = [\"nuget\"]` on a Cargo-only crate — rather than\nc