{"parentUuid":"18ea01c8-a948-4715-b597-d58203e62790","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgN2CbTXLEXMyprRM69G4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B3je3eRx41fHNRX215hkMB","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body-perf.md","content":"`release` and `release --dry-run` spent most of their time waiting on one thing after another. On 10 crates a first-release preview took 2.8 s and on 30 crates 6.7 s; they now take about 1.4 s and 3.5 s.\n\nChanges:\n- Registry lookups for the packages being released run side by side (up to 8), in the name check, the published-version check and the resumable-release check.\n- The per-package history check that stops a rerun from tagging code that was never published runs side by side too. It still starts the same git processes.\n- The workspace is loaded once instead of three times, and the single `git ls-remote` that finds tags missing from `origin` runs beside planning instead of before it.\n\n`cargo info` stays the registry read for Cargo: it honors the user's cargo configuration and credentials, and cargo's own lock limits how much it gains from running in parallel.\n\nTests: an ordering and completeness test for the parallel helper; the existing release and tag-warning tests cover the rest.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":785,"cache_read_input_tokens":328643,"output_tokens":829,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":167},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":785,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":829,"cache_read_input_tokens":328643,"cache_creation_input_tokens":785,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_in