{"parentUuid":"767d9e22-e767-42ef-b36d-cb90b13a7ca0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgN2FtqsJYrWCsvdLKo8v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #364 is open: https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/364. It makes `release` and `release --dry-run` about twice as fast on multi-crate workspaces, and `just ci` passed locally. It merges cleanly with the other open branches.\n\n#359–#363 have all merged, so the stack is done. Only #364 and the release PR #349 are open.\n\n**What I measured:** `release --dry-run` (first release, crates.io) took 2.8 s for 10 crates and 6.7 s for 30. The time was per-package work run one package after another: a `cargo info` lookup, plus about seven git processes for the check that stops a rerun tagging unpublished code.\n\n| Crates | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 10 | 2.8 s | ~1.4 s |\n| 30 | 6.7 s | ~3.5 s |\n\n`status` and `version --dry-run` were already fast, at 10 to 200 ms.\n\n**What changed:**\n- Registry lookups for the packages being released now run up to 8 at a time. That covers the name check, the published-version check and the resumable-release check.\n- The per-package history check also runs concurrently.\n- The workspace loads once instead of three times.\n- The `git ls-remote` tag probe runs beside planning instead of before it.\n\n**What remains:**\n- `cargo info` costs about 100 ms per crate. I kept it because it honors the user's cargo config and credentials. Cargo's own lock also limits how much it gains from running in parallel. Reading the crates.io sparse index directly for public crates would cut that to about 40 ms and parallelize fully. It's a design change, so say if you want it.\n- The history check still starts about seven git processes per package. Batching them into a few processes is the next big win and is more work.\n\nNext I'm looking at that batching and dogfooding other ecosystems. I'll write up whatever turns up.\n\nresult: PR #364 opened, making release and release --dry-run about twice as fast on multi-crate workspaces (10 crates 2.8 s → 1.4 s, 30 crates 6.7 s → 3.5 s), with full local CI passing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":647,"cache_read_input_tokens":330464,"output_tokens":834,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":132},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":647,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":834,"cache_read_input_tokens":330464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":647,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":647},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8f9cab2e-1051-48c8-995b-50d284815396","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgN2FtXmU9eQ5zrVo7sFJ","requestRef":"d29f5615-5b1d-49d2-983c-76c7574a180d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ef3915e2-e1d9-4337-80eb-83b4e95171e3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T00:38:56.763Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/measure","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
