{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","hash":"dd820bc58e2c7a1fe1d5c9b0dd1661078512f6f5cda432e48045703257bb808b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"CI is green. This builds on #364, so I'll open it as the next PR in a native stack."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018embp7RkP48Ugqj5vMXYAX","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body-batch.md","content":"The check that stops a rerun from tagging code that was never published started about seven git processes per package on every `release` and `release --dry-run`. On 10 crates that was about 78; it is now about 33.\n\nIt now reads like `status` does: every manifest at `HEAD` in one `git cat-file --batch`, each package's candidate version commit and its parent in one batched read, and all package directories compared by tree id in one `git cat-file --batch-check`. Each package still makes one `git log`. The result is unchanged: the same packages are reported with the same version commit.\n\nBuilds on the parallel-lookup change: it stacks on that PR.\n\nTests: the existing version-commit tests (inherited versions, merged release branches, a version set long ago, a commit in another package) pass unchanged. The test git runners that wrap real git now support piped input, as the real runner does.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015hV73XczcE2MenHZxCYY2G","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main && zsh /tmp/claude-501/ship.sh perf/batch-version-commit origin/perf/measure \"perf(release): read a package's version history in batches\" /tmp/claude-501/body-batch.md \"Read manifests, version commits and package trees with batched git reads instead of seven processes per package.\" . 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Commit, push and open the stacked PR","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
