{"parentUuid":"9c730102-cef6-4389-98c5-db0726c0db58","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01471xuinAhN28oWM8UBWX64","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"158bbe6a-33fb-4868-890b-9afa6315bc0e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:38:00.695Z","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/batch-version-commit","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"158bbe6a-33fb-4868-890b-9afa6315bc0e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgNBLSs85NzUXfuzDjhF4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #365 is open as a native stack on #364 (stack #366): https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/365. `just ci` passed locally.\n\n#365 replaces the roughly seven git processes per package in the \"published version left behind\" check with batched reads, using the same primitives `status` and the changed-package check already use. The architecture rule \"all VCS reads go through `GitAccess`\" still holds, and the result is the same: the same packages are reported with the same version commit. The existing tests for inherited versions, merged release branches and long-ago versions pass unchanged.\n\n| Per 10-crate first-release preview | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Git processes | ~78 | ~33 |\n\nThe remaining git processes are one `git log` per package, which run in parallel. The ones beyond that are fixed costs.\n\nWall-clock timing is noisy right now because the `cargo info` calls to crates.io are slow and variable, so I'm relying on the process counts rather than the clock for this PR. Cargo lookups, about 100 ms each, are now the main per-package cost.\n\nOpen PRs: #364 and #365 in the stack, plus the release PR #349.\n\nNext I'm looking at the cargo lookup cost. Reading the crates.io sparse index directly for public crates would be the fix. It changes how Callisto authenticates and which tool it trusts for lookups, so I'll write up the trade-off first rather than just doing it.\n\nresult: PR #365 opened and stacked on #364, cutting git processes in the release history check from about 78 to about 33 for 10 crates, with full local CI passing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":377,"cache_read_input_tokens":370416,"output_tokens":528,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":377,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":528,"cache_read_input_tokens":370416,"cache_creation_input_tokens":377,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":377},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e79c3e59-a9df-4a16-b5a0-22cd14e24ce1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNBLSYXW1LajN2K5hpHb","requestRef":"3063c765-f330-4b01-844c-646a536f9ebf","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"35042f64-519c-4c16-bf25-eb298be7fefb","timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:38:00.694Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/batch-version-commit","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
