{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","hash":"0754c567c3d760639a234eb960c4e3e00973cafa123e5f49f458a7318e912fcb","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PKZXVk2j8uVpp1jAvyHuTB","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body-patience.md","content":"With the network down, `release --dry-run` on 10 crates took 61 seconds to print its plan. The wait was the registry name check, which is advisory and was waiting out the full retry schedule that the checks a release depends on use.\n\nThe name check now waits at most one second between its own tries: one retry past a transient failure, then it reports nothing and the plan comes out. The same run takes 2.8 s. The checks a release depends on keep the full schedule.\n\nTest hermeticity: the local-release unit tests ran a real `cargo info` against crates.io. Their git runner now answers a registry lookup as an unpublished crate would. A new test pins that an unreachable registry costs the name check exactly one retry and does not stop the plan.\n\nStacked on the batched-history PR.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y6Jc4DnvqGFs2uCKaYeZEc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main && zsh /tmp/claude-501/ship.sh fix/advisory-check-patience origin/perf/batch-version-commit \"fix(release): do not wait out the retry schedule on an advisory registry check\" /tmp/claude-501/body-patience.md \"Give the advisory name check one retry instead of the full schedule, and keep local-release tests off the network.\" . 2>&1 | tail -2; gh stack link --base main 364 365 367 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Ship and extend the stack","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
