{"parentUuid":"13e6efcb-3a09-4e9d-88e7-8c4e8454edf6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgNKYV8588NFWd2zdPtkz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The conflicts are resolved. #365 was the one in conflict, and #364, #365, #367 and #349 now show no conflict. Their states read \"UNSTABLE\" or \"CLEAN\", which means checks are running or passed, not blocked.\n\n- **Cause:** #364's branch was rebased onto the new `main`, so its commits got new hashes and #365 no longer matched its base. The only real conflict was `version_commit.rs`.\n- **Fix:** I merged the new base into #365 and kept #365's batched version of that file. It replaces #364's parallel version and is a strict improvement on it.\n- **Stack:** I then merged #365 into #367. No force-push on either branch.\n- **Tests:** graph unit tests pass on both branches (971 on #365, 972 on #367).\n\nMerge in stack order: #364, then #365, then #367.\n\nresult: Resolved the merge conflict on #365 by keeping its batched history check, merged it up into #367, and all open PRs are mergeable with graph tests passing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":480,"cache_read_input_tokens":394148,"output_tokens":332,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":480,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":332,"cache_read_input_tokens":394148,"cache_creation_input_tokens":480,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":480},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b84b6d5d-6b87-4e87-8684-662a43fb8f43","apiBlockInde