{"parentUuid":"02bae33e-cba4-4c8f-8af0-cac68dcdc902","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_014wnjomByGkLpeKPD8B1fQX","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e8c695bc-85e4-47b0-af12-ec645a5a1cac","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:21:55.127Z","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"ci/release-verify-linters","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"e8c695bc-85e4-47b0-af12-ec645a5a1cac","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPGADNoiB2T4mUzbiHpA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's what's left, based on what I just inspected in the repo and the last coverage run.\n\n**Releases first:** #368 is open and unblocks the release workflow. Every Release run since last night failed because the verify job lacked the workflow linters. Merge it first, then the release PR opens.\n\n**Test coverage (91–95% by crate; the gate is 90% overall)**\n\n| Priority | Where | Why it matters |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | `cascade.rs`, 71% (125 lines missed) | Core of version bumping: dependency ranges, fixed and linked groups |\n| 2 | `release/capability.rs`, 79% | The trust and staleness checks that guard every release |\n| 3 | CLI `release.rs`, 80% | The execute path: receipts, partial failures and reruns |\n| 4 | CLI `add.rs`, 73% | The first command a new user runs |\n| 5 | `registry.rs`, `binding.rs`, `release_decision.rs` | Registry and binding edge cases |\n| 6 | `manifests/cargo.rs` and `npm.rs`, 87–89% | Hand-formatted manifests |\n\nCoverage numbers aren't the aim. For `cascade.rs` I'd write property tests that bump any DAG and check the invariants: no dependent is left declaring a range its dependency left, and fixed-group versions stay equal. That finds bugs where line coverage only touches code. There are 7 `proptest` suites today, none for cascading.\n\n**Rust setup vs best practice**\n\nWhat's already solid: edition 2024, MSRV 1.96 with a CI job, `unsafe_code = \"forbid\"`, workspace lints, `unwrap_used` denied in lib/bin code, cargo-deny and a separate advisories workflow, doc build with warnings denied, fuzz targets compiled in CI, nextest, 90% coverage gate.\n\nGaps:\n1. **Not in CI:** `cargo semver-checks` and `cargo machete`. Both recipes exist but only run by hand. Also not in CI: `cargo mutants`, which is slow, so it should be a weekly job.\n2. **Per-crate coverage is non-blocking.** `callisto-manifests` is at 89%, under the 90% target, and CI only warns.\n3. **Lints:** only `clippy::all` plus a few denies. Worth adding `dbg_macro`, `todo`, `unimplemented` and `print_stdout` on library crates.\n4. **Fuzzing:** 4 targets, compile-checked only, never run. A short scheduled run (~2 minutes each) on the manifest parsers would be useful.\n5. **Windows:** unsupported and untested. It's documented as unsupported in `stability.md`. Say so if the v1 promise should include it, since npm and Python users are often on Windows.\n6. **Supply chain:** no SBOM or build provenance on release binaries. Attestations exist for artifacts but I haven't verified they cover the CLI binaries.\n\n**Proposed order (one PR each):**\n1. CI: add `machete` and `semver-checks`, make per-crate coverage blocking.\n2. Property tests for the version cascade.\n3. Tests for `capability.rs` staleness and the `release.rs` execute path.\n4. Lint hardening, applied crate by crate.\n5. Weekly mutants and fuzz jobs.\n\nI'll start with 1 and 2 unless you want a different order.\n\nresult: PR #368 opened to unblock the failing release workflow, and the hardening, test-coverage and Rust-practice gaps are audited and prioritized."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":901,"cache_read_input_tokens":416430,"output_tokens":1196,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":901,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1196,"cache_read_input_tokens":416430,"cache_creation_input_tokens":901,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":901},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_t