{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","hash":"5ccca1ad70c6ced75c3fe8f5f252bea1dc98458662fa884400a6c5f3d7df861b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"`callisto-manifests` is at 89.22%, about 21 lines short of 90. I'll close that gap with real tests rather than lowering the gate. Finding the uncovered lines."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MTM21ssER9TxD9h8kLm9ci","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/uncovered.py","content":"import sys\n\nwant = sys.argv[1]\ncur = None\nmiss = []\nfor line in open(\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/lcov.info\"):\n    line = line.strip()\n    if line.startswith(\"SF:\"):\n        cur = line[3:]\n        miss = []\n    elif line.startswith(\"DA:\") and cur and cur.endswith(want):\n        n, hits = line[3:].split(\",\")[:2]\n        if hits == \"0\":\n            miss.append(int(n))\n    elif line == \"end_of_record\" and cur and cur.endswith(want):\n        ranges = []\n        for n in miss:\n            if ranges and n == ranges[-1][1] + 1:\n                ranges[-1][1] = n\n            else:\n                ranges.append([n, n])\n        print(want, \", \".join(f\"{a}-{b}\" if a != b else str(a) for a, b in ranges))\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017qr1Dh62gt2LzReiGiyEUS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main && cargo llvm-cov report --lcov --output-path lcov.info >/dev/null 2>&1; for f in callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs callisto-manifests/src/npm.rs callisto-manifests/src/python.rs callisto-manifests/src/lib.rs callisto-manifests/src/common.rs; do python3 -I /tmp/claude-501/uncovered.py crates/${f#callisto-manifests/} 2>/dev/null; python3 -I /tmp/claude-501/uncovered.py ${f#callisto-manifests/} | cut -c1-300; done","description":"List uncovered line ranges in the manifests crate","dan