{"parentUuid":"fee1a74d-d38c-447a-b3aa-9e4626bb0706","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPHNh68xZ21whAbRTvF1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VPL52MExyhPrj3Kyd9Yah5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body-hyg.md","content":"CI now enforces three checks that existed as recipes but ran by hand, and `callisto-manifests` gains the tests it needed to pass the per-crate coverage gate.\n\n- Unused dependencies: `cargo machete` runs in CI. It found `camino` and `thiserror` unused in `callisto-manifests`; both are removed.\n- Shipped features: `just features-boundary` fails if the dev-only `test-util` feature appears anywhere in `callisto-cli`'s build, so the published binaries cannot carry it. They carry every other feature their crates default to.\n- Public API: `cargo semver-checks` runs on the release PR, where versions have moved, and compares the public API with the published one. On an ordinary PR a version has not moved, so any addition would fail it.\n- Per-crate coverage is now blocking at 90%. `callisto-manifests` was at 89.2%, so it gets tests for the behavior that decides what ships, not for the number: which `publish` values make a crate publishable, `private` and `publishConfig` in `package.json`, a truncated `package.json`, missing and invalid name and version, the workspace version with and without a byte order mark and when invalid, and the refusal to update optional Cargo dependencies. It is now at 90.7%.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":430,"cache_read_input_tokens":455444,"output_tokens":777,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":430,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":777,"cache_read_input_tokens":455444,"cache_creation_input_tokens":430,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":430},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VPL52MExyhPrj3Kyd9Yah5":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body-hyg.md","content":"CI now enforces three checks that existed as recipes but ran by hand, and `callisto-manifests` gains the tests it needed to pass the per-crate coverage gate.\n\n- Unused dependencies: `cargo machete` runs in CI. It found `camino` and `thiserror` unused in `callisto-manifests`; both are removed.\n- Shipped features: `just features-boundary` fails if the dev-only `test-util` feature appears anywhere in `callisto-cli`'s build, so the published binaries cannot carry it. They carry every other feature their crates default to.\n- Public API: `cargo semver-checks` runs on the release PR, where versions have moved, and compares the public API with the published one. On an ordinary PR a version has not moved, so any addition would fail it.\n- Per-crate coverage is now blocking at 90%. `callisto-manifests` was at 89.2%, so it gets tests for the behavior that decides what ships, not for the number: which `publish` values make a crate publishable, `private` and `publishConfig` in `package.json`, a truncated `package.json`, missing and invalid name and version, the workspace version with and without a byte order mark and when invalid, and the refusal to update optional Cargo dependencies. It is now at 90.7%.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e7f6e7c5-148b-431f-8e85-c47e2d9fa16d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPHNgj4642JhQoUAwdHA","requestRef":"98519131-6912-4d46-800e-cdb34ad543ed","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9300725f-5948-410e-9af3-5a874c6b4343","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:37:44.836Z","ad