{"parentUuid":"789306c4-8023-474b-9969-18ddd4018722","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPHTryr9BxyfZy4N22CF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing reads that count line, so I'll drop it. Now the README quick start to match the real first-run flow, then CONTRIBUTING."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1633,"cache_read_input_tokens":464243,"output_tokens":1687,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":427},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1633,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1687,"cache_read_input_tokens":464243,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1633,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1633},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"2780a6a4-d9b0-4265-998a-07e93de38537","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPHTraXcBP3X2tEU8idD","requestRef":"893972e8-1f90-44e1-ae4b-325c0dd5c0fa","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"72a8a593-dd8f-49e7-b97b-2f981073d222","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:38:55.346Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"docs/refresh-readme-contributing","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"72a8a593-dd8f-49e7-b97b-2f981073d222","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPHTryr9BxyfZy4N22CF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FZubDTJHvUVXTq6vicGZsz","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/README.md","old_string":"Start in a Git repository with an `origin` push URL and crates.io credentials. This registry-only example publishes a crate and creates a tag; it does not build assets or create a GitHub Release. See [releasing](docs/releasing.md) for CI and product releases.\n\n```bash\n# 1. Scaffold callisto.toml and .changeset/ in the workspace root\ncallisto init --yes --no-workflow\n\n# 2. Record a pending change against a package\ncallisto add --package cargo/my-crate:minor --summary \"Add authentication middleware\"\n\n# 3. See pending changesets and the version bumps they imply\ncallisto status\n\n# 4. Commit the configuration and pending change\ngit add callisto.toml .changeset/\ngit commit -m \"chore: configure releases and record pending changes\"\n\n# 5. Consume changesets, bump manifests, update changelogs and lockfiles\ncallisto version\n\n# 6. Commit the staged release changes; release requires a clean checkout\ngit commit -m \"chore(release): version packages\"\n\n# 7. Preview, then publish\ncallisto release --dry-run\ncallisto release\n```\n\nRun `callisto --help` for prerelease mode, snapshots, CI checks, JSON output, and shell completions.","new_string":"Start in a Git repository with an `origin` push URL and registry credentials. This example publishes from your machine; to publish from CI instead, keep the workflow `init` writes and see [releasing](docs/releasing.md).\n\n```bash\n# 1. Detect packages, write callisto.toml and .changeset/, preview the first release.\n#    With a GitHub origin it also writes the release workflow, and it prints what to do next.\ncallisto init --yes --no-workflow\n\n# 2. Record a pending change against a package\ncallisto add --package cargo/my-crate:minor --summary \"Add authentication middleware\"\n\n# 3. See pending changesets and the version bumps they imply\ncallisto status\n\n# 4. Commit the configuration and pending change\ngit add callisto.toml .changeset/\ngit commit -m \"chore: configure releases and record pending changes\"\n\n# 5. Consume changesets, bump manifests, update changelogs and lockfiles\ncallisto version\n\n# 6. Commit the staged release changes; release requires a clean checkout\ngit commit -m \"chore(release): version packages\"\n\n# 7. Preview, then publish\ncallisto release --dry-run\ncallisto release\n```\n\nDrop `--no-workflow` to publish from GitHub Actions instead: a push to the default branch opens a release PR, and merging it publishes. A first release of a Cargo crate needs a `description` and a `license`; Callisto stops with a fix before publishing anything if they are missing.\n\nRun `callisto --help` for prerelease mode, snapshots, CI checks, JSON output, and shell completions."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1633,"cache_read_input_tokens":464243,"output_tokens":1687,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":427},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1633,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1687,"cache_read_input_tokens":464243,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1633,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1633},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FZubDTJHvUVXTq6vicGZsz":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/README.md","old_string":"Start in a Git repository with an `origin` push URL and crates.io credentials. This registry-only example publishes a crate and creates a tag; it does not build assets or create a GitHub Release. See [releasing](docs/releasing.md) for CI and product releases.\n\n```bash\n# 1. Scaffold callisto.toml and .changeset/ in the workspace root\ncallisto init --yes --no-workflow\n\n# 2. Record a pending change against a package\ncallisto add --package cargo/my-crate:minor --summary \"Add authentication middleware\"\n\n# 3. See pending changesets and the version bumps they imply\ncallisto status\n\n# 4. Commit the configuration and pending change\ngit add callisto.toml .changeset/\ngit commit -m \"chore: configure releases and record pending changes\"\n\n# 5. Consume changesets, bump manifests, update changelogs and lockfiles\ncallisto version\n\n# 6. Commit the staged release changes; release requires a clean checkout\ngit commit -m \"chore(release): version packages\"\n\n# 7. Preview, then publish\ncallisto release --dry-run\ncallisto release\n```\n\nRun `callisto --help` for prerelease mode, snapshots, CI checks, JSON output, and shell completions.","new_str":"Start in a Git repository with an `origin` push URL and registry credentials. This example publishes from your machine; to publish from CI instead, keep the workflow `init` writes and see [releasing](docs/releasing.md).\n\n```bash\n# 1. Detect packages, write callisto.toml and .changeset/, preview the first release.\n#    With a GitHub origin it also writes the release workflow, and it prints what to do next.\ncallisto init --yes --no-workflow\n\n# 2. Record a pending change against a package\ncallisto add --package cargo/my-crate:minor --summary \"Add authentication middleware\"\n\n# 3. See pending changesets and the version bumps they imply\ncallisto status\n\n# 4. Commit the configuration and pending change\ngit add callisto.toml .changeset/\ngit commit -m \"chore: configure releases and record pending changes\"\n\n# 5. Consume changesets, bump manifests, update changelogs and lockfiles\ncallisto version\n\n# 6. Commit the staged release changes; release requires a clean checkout\ngit commit -m \"chore(release): version packages\"\n\n# 7. Preview, then publish\ncallisto release --dry-run\ncallisto release\n```\n\nDrop `--no-workflow` to publish from GitHub Actions instead: a push to the default branch opens a release PR, and merging it publishes. A first release of a Cargo crate needs a `description` and a `license`; Callisto stops with a fix before publishing anything if they are missing.\n\nRun `callisto --help` for prerelease mode, snapshots, CI checks, JSON output, and shell completions."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"2780a6a4-d9b0-4265-998a-07e93de38537","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgPHTraXcBP3X2tEU8idD","requestRef":"893972e8-1f90-44e1-ae4b-325c0dd5c0fa","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7c78166d-de46-40ae-a6c7-1b96e873d860","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:39:00.384Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"docs/refresh-readme-contributing","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
