{"parentUuid":"8e7062cf-8d6b-454d-b5a6-92b78df36167","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPHV1t9VrpoGNgZVLAHm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Gk6vk1T8ztxBjAWMatPRVv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np=\"CONTRIBUTING.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\n\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- Rust toolchain: pinned in `rust-toolchain.toml`, installed via `rustup`.\n- [`just`](https://github.com/casey/just): command runner for all workspace recipes.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"- Rust toolchain: pinned in `rust-toolchain.toml`, installed via `rustup`.\n- [`just`](https://github.com/casey/just): command runner for all workspace recipes.\n- Cargo tools the recipes call: `cargo-nextest`, `cargo-llvm-cov`, `cargo-deny`, `cargo-machete` and `cargo-semver-checks`.\n- Workflow linters `zizmor` and `actionlint`: tests that lint the workflow `callisto init` generates run them, and fail under CI when they are missing (locally they skip).\n\"\"\")\n\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"| `just coverage-per-crate [threshold]` | Same profile data, gated per crate instead of workspace-total (CI runs this non-blocking today; default threshold 90) |\"\"\",\"\"\"| `just coverage-per-crate [threshold]` | Same profile data, gated per crate instead of workspace-total; CI runs it blocking at 90 |\n| `just machete` | Unused dependencies (`cargo machete`); CI runs it |\n| `just features-boundary` | Fails if the dev-only `test-util` feature reaches the shipped `callisto-cli` build; CI runs it |\n| `just check-api` | Public API compared with the published crates (`cargo semver-checks`); CI runs it on the release PR, where versions have moved |\n| `just bench` | Wall time and git process counts for `status`, `version --dry-run` and `release --dry-run` over generated workspaces |\n| `just fuzz-check` | Compiles the fuzz targets so they cannot rot; CI runs it |\"\"\")\n\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"Maintainer-only recipes not part of the normal PR loop: `mutants` (mutation testing), `machete` (unused deps), `check-api` (SemVer diff via `cargo-semver-checks`), `fuzz`, `provider-fixtures`/`provider-contract` (re-capture/verify the real-provider test fixtures under `testing/fixtures/`).\"\"\",\"\"\"Maintainer-only recipes not part of the normal PR loop: `mutants` (mutation testing), `fuzz` (runs a fuzz target; needs nightly and `cargo-fuzz`), `provider-fixtures`/`provider-contract` (re-capture/verify the real-provider test fixtures under `testing/fixtures/`).\"\"\")\n\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- **`coverage`** — `just coverage 90` (workspace line coverage must not regress below 90%); per-crate coverage runs non-blocking\"\"\",\"\"\"- **`coverage`** — `just coverage 90` (workspace line coverage must not regress below 90%) and `just coverage-per-crate 90` (each crate too)\n- **`hygiene`** — `just machete`, `just features-boundary`, and on the release PR `just check-api`\"\"\")\n\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"Before opening a PR: run `just ci` locally\"\"\",\"\"\"Tests earn their place by covering a behavior, an edge case or an error state, not a line. A change that adds a diagnostic code also adds its row to [docs/errors.md](docs/errors.md); a test fails without it.\n\nBefore opening a PR: run `just ci` locally\"\"\")\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -c \"hygiene\\|features-boundary\" CONTRIBUTING.md","description":"Update CONTRIBUTING setup, recipes and checklist","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":544,"cache_read_input_tokens":468058,"output_tokens":1648,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":544,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1648,"cache_read_input_tokens":4680