{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","hash":"5abeec53e146cc0b40e5c7ee59687ac776bd10255260f0a5cb42dbc5f316d30b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The claim is accurate. Applying the CONTRIBUTING edits one at a time."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012vknrTegVL5TBGVtVs2nsh","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/CONTRIBUTING.md","old_string":"- [`just`](https://github.com/casey/just): command runner for all workspace recipes.\n","new_str":"- [`just`](https://github.com/casey/just): command runner for all workspace recipes.\n- Cargo tools the recipes call: `cargo-nextest`, `cargo-llvm-cov`, `cargo-deny`, `cargo-machete` and `cargo-semver-checks`.\n- Workflow linters `zizmor` and `actionlint`: tests that lint the workflow `callisto init` generates run them. A missing one skips the check on your machine and fails the test under CI.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VMLEzAdCAesGMXUFBAZ4UT","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/CONTRIBUTING.md","old_string":"| `just coverage-per-crate [threshold]` | Same profile data, gated per crate instead of workspace-total (CI runs this non-blocking today; default threshold 90) |","new_str":"| `just coverage-per-crate [threshold]` | Same profile data, gated per crate instead of workspace-total; CI runs it blocking at 90 |\n| `just machete` | Unused dependencies (`cargo machete`); CI runs it |\n| `just features-boundary` | Fails if the dev-only `test-util` feature reaches the shipped `callisto-cli` build; CI runs it |\n| `just check-api` | Public API compared with the published crates (`cargo semver-checks`); CI runs it on the release PR, where versions have moved |\n| `just bench` | Wall time and process counts for `status`, `version --dry-run` and `release --dry-run` over generated workspaces |\n| `just fuzz-check` | Compiles the fuzz targets so they cannot rot; CI runs it |"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014YmydCvAUuDC8ZhuBYn629","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/CONTRIBUTING.md","old_string":"`mutants` (mutation testing), `machete` (unused deps), `check-api` (SemVer diff via `cargo-semver-checks`), `fuzz`, `provider-fixtures`","new_str":"`mutants` (mutation testing), `fuzz` (runs a fuzz target; needs nightly and `cargo-fuzz`), `provider-fixtures`"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01897WBYu92UCWev7prk3ypu","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/CONTRIBUTING.md","old_string":"- **`coverage`** — `just coverage 90` (workspace line coverage must not regress below 90%); per-crate coverage runs non-blocking","new_str":"- **`coverage`** — `just coverage 90` (workspace line coverage must not regress below 90%) and `just coverage-per-crate 90` (each crate too)\n- **`hygiene`** — `just machete`, `just features-boundary`, and on the release PR `just check-api`"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011mZCw2mYhBwFn8L6Kt84GU","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/CONTRIBUTING.md","old_string":"Before opening a PR: run `just ci` locally","new_str":"Tests earn their place by covering a behavior, an edge case or an error state, not a line. A change that adds a diagnostic code also adds its row to [docs/errors.md](docs/errors.md); a test fails without it.\n\nBefore opening a PR: run `just ci` locally"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","hash":"38a35175d51dce2acf44ba6d0cf97e57a060eeee9081e0659439c0d51e45a8b9","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The task tools haven't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using TaskCreate to add new tasks and TaskUpdate to update task status (set to in_progress when starting, completed when done). Also consider cleaning up the task list if it has become stale. Only use these if relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\n\n\n<total_tokens>14945596 tokens left</total_tokens>\n\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."}]}}
