{"parentUuid":"84b6bfa7-3d91-4421-8f91-58349551143a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPHX4K4ghqDonmGje7gd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TZVyqVGUFEf7Dvfiyx5FB7","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/architecture/release.md","offset":66,"limit":16},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2224,"cache_read_input_tokens":471373,"output_tokens":323,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":161},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2224,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":323,"cache_read_input_tokens":471373,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2224,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2224},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TZVyqVGUFEf7Dvfiyx5FB7":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/architecture/release.md","offset":66,"limit":16}},"serverClassifierRequest":"408958da-e405-400b-836b-9ae406b92683","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgPHX3s2ci6V76DimoqRj","requestRef":"e0942181-8c30-4c14-9a11-e96216873532","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"563430dd-bf7d-43c4-9802-30cffcf81554","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:39:36.970Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"docs/refresh-readme-contributing","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"563430dd-bf7d-43c4-9802-30cffcf81554","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fbb155ba-b167-49bf-8715-f1b81bf02c2f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TZVyqVGUFEf7Dvfiyx5FB7","type":"tool_result","content":"66\t- `ProviderEvidenceV1` is closed and per role: registry version, git tag peeled commit, forge release tag and draft flag, artifact size and sha256.\n67\t- `ReleaseOperationObservationV1::new` rejects evidence whose shape does not belong to the operation's role; deserialization goes through it too.\n68\t- Proof tokens: `AbsentProof` is minted only from `Absent`, `ExactEvidence` only from `Exact`.\n69\t- `execute_release` observes each operation once before its effect: exact is adopted, absent is performed then confirmed, anything else stops the run before the effect.\n70\t- An npm registry publish is the exception to \"then confirmed\": it is issued, stays `Attempting`, and another npm publish may follow it. When nothing else can start, the executor looks at all issued publishes together until each is shown or the longest `confirm-timeout` is spent. That window is one `ConfirmationWave`: it opens when the first publish is issued, is measured on the provider set's clock so looking counts, and a publish shown along the way does not restart it. Each look is given the window that is left as its patience, so a registry that asks for long waits between tries cannot hold a look past the window; a look that has none left tries once. The tag, release draft, uploads and publication wait for the confirmation, so nothing is announced before the registry shows the version. Cargo and PyPI publishes are confirmed as they are published (PyPI completion is a file set, not a version).\n71\t\n72\tProvider reads use native tools for Cargo and npm, and `curl` for PyPI's PEP 691 JSON simple index:\n73\t\n74\t- Cargo: `cargo info NAME@VERSION --registry REGISTRY` runs from the source root. Matching `version:` means exact; exit 101 with ``could not find `NAME@VERSION` `` means absent. Other results are indeterminate. Yanked versions are invisible to `cargo info`; a rejected publish ends without a receipt.\n75\t- npm: `npm view NAME@VERSION --json --fetch-retries=0`.\n76\t- PyPI: a matching file means exact; 404 or no match means absent; transport failure or non-JSON means indeterminate. Yanked matches count as absent. Before an effect, `release execute` also builds the release's files once into a temporary directory and compares their names with the index, so a partly uploaded release uploads only what is missing and is satisfied only when the whole set is there.\n77\t\n78\tAdopting a version that is already published is by design, so a rerun can finish a half-done release. Because a foreign package would be adopted the same way, a Cargo or npm adoption also reads the repository the registry records for that version (`repository:` in `cargo info`, `repository` in `npm view`) and warns, without blocking, when it names a different repository from `origin`. A registry that records none, or a failed read, says nothing; PyPI's simple index records no repository, so it is not checked.\n79\t\n80\tThese reads are version-level checks, not proof of identical bytes or the npm dist-tag. Registry endpoints must be HTTPS. Read-only observations before an effect retry 429, 5xx, rate-limited 403, and transport failures with backoff and `Retry-After`. Effects are never blindly retried; outbound commands have deadlines.\n81\t"}]},"uuid":"f4a12cbb-38e4-4e3c-9ce4-f59f84f8f136","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:39:37.067Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/architecture/release.md","content":"- `ProviderEvidenceV1` is closed and per role: registry version, git tag peeled commit, forge release tag and draft flag, artifact size and sha256.\n- `ReleaseOperationObservationV1::new` rejects evidence whose shape does not belong to the operation's role; deserialization goes through it too.\n- Proof tokens: `AbsentProof` is minted only from `Absent`, `ExactEvidence` only from `Exact`.\n- `execute_release` observes each operation once before its effect: exact is adopted, absent is performed then confirmed, anything else stops the run before the effect.\n- An npm registry publish is the exception to \"then confirmed\": it is issued, stays `Attempting`, and another npm publish may follow it. When nothing else can start, the executor looks at all issued publishes together until each is shown or the longest `confirm-timeout` is spent. That window is one `ConfirmationWave`: it opens when the first publish is issued, is measured on the provider set's clock so looking counts, and a publish shown along the way does not restart it. Each look is given the window that is left as its patience, so a registry that asks for long waits between tries cannot hold a look past the window; a look that has none left tries once. The tag, release draft, uploads and publication wait for the confirmation, so nothing is announced before the registry shows the version. Cargo and PyPI publishes are confirmed as they are published (PyPI completion is a file set, not a version).\n\nProvider reads use native tools for Cargo and npm, and `curl` for PyPI's PEP 691 JSON simple index:\n\n- Cargo: `cargo info NAME@VERSION --registry REGISTRY` runs from the source root. Matching `version:` means exact; exit 101 with ``could not find `NAME@VERSION` `` means absent. Other results are indeterminate. Yanked versions are invisible to `cargo info`; a rejected publish ends without a receipt.\n- npm: `npm view NAME@VERSION --json --fetch-retries=0`.\n- PyPI: a matching file means exact; 404 or no match means absent; transport failure or non-JSON means indeterminate. Yanked matches count as absent. Before an effect, `release execute` also builds the release's files once into a temporary directory and compares their names with the index, so a partly uploaded release uploads only what is missing and is satisfied only when the whole set is there.\n\nAdopting a version that is already published is by design, so a rerun can finish a half-done release. Because a foreign package would be adopted the same way, a Cargo or npm adoption also reads the repository the registry records for that version (`repository:` in `cargo info`, `repository` in `npm view`) and warns, without blocking, when it names a different repository from `origin`. A registry that records none, or a failed read, says nothing; PyPI's simple index records no repository, so it is not checked.\n\nThese reads are version-level checks, not proof of identical bytes or the npm dist-tag. Registry endpoints must be HTTPS. Read-only observations before an effect retry 429, 5xx, rate-limited 403, and transport failures with backoff and `Retry-After`. Effects are never blindly retried; outbound commands have deadlines.\n","numLines":16,"startLine":66,"totalLines":131}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"563430dd-bf7d-43c4-9802-30cffcf81554","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"docs/refresh-readme-contributing","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
