"perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"docs/refresh-readme-contributing","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"f3de9604-5665-4e00-a975-0033751fec63","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fbb155ba-b167-49bf-8715-f1b81bf02c2f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RB4YpQ8KSNXrfmFtUddQyj","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/architecture/release.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"acf1148f-56a2-4cdd-88ee-aa6039418c45","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:39:43.675Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/architecture/release.md","oldString":"These reads are version-level checks, not proof of identical bytes or the npm dist-tag.","newString":"Planning looks at many packages at once, so its reads are built to scale with the number of packages, not to add a process or a round trip per package:\n\n- Observations that the plan makes before any effect (the published-version check, the name check, the resumable-release check) are independent reads and run side by side, up to eight at a time, in package order.\n- The name check is advisory, so it waits at most one second between its own tries and says nothing when a registry does not answer; the checks a release depends on keep the full retry schedule. An unreachable network therefore costs a preview seconds, not a minute.\n- Git history for all packages is read in batches (one `cat-file --batch` for manifests, one for each package's candidate version commit and its parent, one `cat-file --batch-check` that compares package directories by tree id), plus one `git log` per package.\n- The workspace is loaded once per command, and the one `git ls-remote` that finds tags missing from `origin` runs beside planning.\n- `just bench` reports wall time and git process counts per command; a change that adds a git process per package fails review.\n\nThese reads are version-level checks, not proof of identical bytes or the npm dist-tag.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":77,"oldLines":6,"newStart":77,"newLines":14,"lines":[" "," Adopting a version that is already published is by design, so a rerun can finish a half-done release. Because a foreign package would be adopted the same way, a Cargo or npm adoption also reads the repository the registry records for that version (`repository:` in `cargo info`, `repository` in `npm view`) and warns, without blocking, when it names a different repository from `origin`. A registry that records none, or a failed read, says nothing; PyPI's simple index records no repository, so it is not checked."," ","+Planning looks at many packages at once, so its reads are built to scale with the number of packages, not to add a process or a round trip per package:","+","+- Observations that the plan makes before any effect (the published-version check, the name check, the resumable-release check) are independent reads and run side by side, up to eight at a time, in package order.","+- The name check is advisory, so it waits at most one second between its own tries and says nothing when a registry does not answer; the checks a release depends on keep the full retry schedule. An unreachable network therefore costs a preview seconds, not a minute.","+- Git history for all packages is read in batches (one `cat-file --batch` for manifests, one for each package's candidate version commit and its parent, one `cat-file --batch-check` that compares package directories by tree id), plus one `git log` per package.","+- The workspace is loaded once per command, and the one `git ls-remote` that finds tags missing from `origin` runs beside planning.","+- `just bench` reports wall time and git process counts per command; a change that adds a git process per package fails review.","+"," These reads are version-level checks, not proof of identical bytes or the npm dist-tag. Registry endpoints must be HTTPS. Read-only observations before an effect retry 429, 5xx, rate-limited 403, and transport failures with backoff and `Retry-After`. Effects are never blindly retried; outbound commands have deadlines."," "," After a registry publish the version may not be readable yet: npm serves a package's document with `max-age=300`, a missing package's 404 included, so a read just before the publish can answer stale for five minutes. The confirmation therefore waits by time, not tries, treating absent and unreachable as lag until the registry's window (`confirm-timeout`, default 6 minutes for npm and PyPI, 2 for Cargo) is spent, then fails with E157. An exact version or a conflict ends the wait at once."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f3de9604-5665-4e00-a975-0033751fec63","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"docs/refresh-readme-contributing","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
