{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","hash":"2cd0e63f9a766408447d32742fdb6ff56ecd5e945b92cbe14ef4b3be6d32db5b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RB4YpQ8KSNXrfmFtUddQyj","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/architecture/release.md","old_string":"These reads are version-level checks, not proof of identical bytes or the npm dist-tag.","new_str":"Planning looks at many packages at once, so its reads are built to scale with the number of packages, not to add a process or a round trip per package:\n\n- Observations that the plan makes before any effect (the published-version check, the name check, the resumable-release check) are independent reads and run side by side, up to eight at a time, in package order.\n- The name check is advisory, so it waits at most one second between its own tries and says nothing when a registry does not answer; the checks a release depends on keep the full retry schedule. An unreachable network therefore costs a preview seconds, not a minute.\n- Git history for all packages is read in batches (one `cat-file --batch` for manifests, one for each package's candidate version commit and its parent, one `cat-file --batch-check` that compares package directories by tree id), plus one `git log` per package.\n- The workspace is loaded once per command, and the one `git ls-remote` that finds tags missing from `origin` runs beside planning.\n- `just bench` reports wall time and git process counts per command; a change that adds a git process per package fails review.\n\nThese reads are version-level checks, not proof of identical bytes or the npm dist-tag."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WNzaxK34ZvZzAbCqDScPB9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main && sed -n 55,62p ARCHITECTURE.md | cut -c1-500","description":"Read the ARCHITECTURE.md git access paragraph","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
