{"parentUuid":"cee2d65f-1df8-4262-b8ac-56d19bffbd6f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPHauPQ1s5N7Dv6Q4Hwg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018xVAB3p9DJMgLhRxZb5St5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body-docs.md","content":"The README, CONTRIBUTING and architecture docs described the project before the recent first-run, performance and CI changes.\n\n- README: the quick start now describes what `callisto init` does today (detects packages, previews the first release, writes the workflow for a GitHub origin and prints next steps), how to publish from GitHub Actions instead, and the Cargo `description` and `license` requirement for a first release.\n- CONTRIBUTING: the tools the recipes and tests need, the new `machete`, `features-boundary`, `check-api`, `bench` and `fuzz-check` recipes, the `hygiene` job, blocking per-crate coverage, and what a test is for (a behavior, edge case or error state, not a line).\n- Architecture: the rules planning reads follow so cost does not grow per package (parallel observations, advisory patience, batched git history, one workspace load), and where `just bench` measures them.\n- `docs/errors.md`: the hand-maintained \"N codes total\" line is gone. Nothing read it, and every PR adding a code conflicted on it.\n\nStacked on the CI hygiene PR, which adds the recipes and jobs these docs describe.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":864,"cache_read_input_tokens":477910,"output_tokens":759,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":864,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":759,"cache_read_input_tok