{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","hash":"5c7972219acc5113c28239b524b4eacb04eae1f671c7c6e6aa70f1352f4930b9","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018xVAB3p9DJMgLhRxZb5St5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body-docs.md","content":"The README, CONTRIBUTING and architecture docs described the project before the recent first-run, performance and CI changes.\n\n- README: the quick start now describes what `callisto init` does today (detects packages, previews the first release, writes the workflow for a GitHub origin and prints next steps), how to publish from GitHub Actions instead, and the Cargo `description` and `license` requirement for a first release.\n- CONTRIBUTING: the tools the recipes and tests need, the new `machete`, `features-boundary`, `check-api`, `bench` and `fuzz-check` recipes, the `hygiene` job, blocking per-crate coverage, and what a test is for (a behavior, edge case or error state, not a line).\n- Architecture: the rules planning reads follow so cost does not grow per package (parallel observations, advisory patience, batched git history, one workspace load), and where `just bench` measures them.\n- `docs/errors.md`: the hand-maintained \"N codes total\" line is gone. Nothing read it, and every PR adding a code conflicted on it.\n\nStacked on the CI hygiene PR, which adds the recipes and jobs these docs describe.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KxDkihWoqygBK3eesheAP2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main && zsh /tmp/claude-501/ship.sh docs/refresh-readme-contributing origin/ci/gate-machete-semver \"docs: refresh the README, contributing guide and architecture notes\" /tmp/claude-501/body-docs.md \"Describe the current first-run flow, CI gates and planning-cost rules; drop the hand-kept error count.\" . 2>&1 | tail -2; gh stack link --base main 369 370 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Ship the docs PR and stack it on #369","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
