{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","hash":"bcb22e9ba2f92d8fc7e3600288cad2858d9249df06db957e2526e033566e3646","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've pinpointed the uncovered lines—a grammar mismatch aborting the cascade, an untestable catalog spec, and a stale linked-group member. Now I'll figure out how to construct specs that trigger these cases.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FYXvyQnKeySS5PD4jLMkXh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main && grep -n \"Catalog(\" crates/callisto-model/src/dependency.rs | head -5; grep -n \"pub struct CatalogRef\\|pub struct Catalog\" -A8 crates/callisto-model/src/dependency.rs | head -14; grep -n \"Catalog\" crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade/tests.rs | head -3; grep -n \"GroupGrammarMismatch\\|GrammarMismatch {\" crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs | head -3","description":"Find how Catalog specs and mismatch errors are shaped","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
