{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","hash":"d39260d322ba73fed42393e1201ab0245e810ca1c8680cb05dbc3b4cc2a23f36","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018FnqUEcaq3EqRgP1edWjmr","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-501/body-casc.md","content":"The version cascade decides which dependents get released and which ranges are rewritten. Its tests were scenario by scenario; these check what a user relies on, over random inputs, plus the error and warning states that had no test.\n\nProperty test, 256 random acyclic dependency graphs with random bases, seeds, cascade mode and bump severity. After every cascade:\n- no dependent declares a range its dependency has left;\n- a dependent whose range stopped covering its dependency is itself released;\n- no version moves backwards;\n- a seeded package keeps at least the severity its changeset gave it;\n- planning twice gives the same plan.\n\nI checked the property can fail: asserting that no rewrite ever happens fails on the first generated graph.\n\nError and warning states, each with its own test:\n- a range in a different version grammar than its dependency stops the cascade with both packages named;\n- a catalog spec warns, names its dependent and is never rewritten;\n- an opaque spec is left alone without a warning;\n- a linked-group member that is not in the workspace is skipped with a warning naming the group and the member.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Pib1JmB83KEeGtTHDgTtWu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main && zsh /tmp/claude-501/ship.sh test/cascade-properties origin/main \"test(cascade): check invariants over random graphs and cover the error and warning states\" /tmp/claude-501/body-casc.md \"Property-test the version cascade over random dependency graphs and cover its grammar-mismatch, catalog, opaque and stale-group-member states.\" .