{"parentUuid":"ab0797b1-f490-4bc6-9545-61eb5986e8ba","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPJEqvLn7R3skgdvgqqv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Three PRs are open: #369 and #370 (stacked) and #372 (independent, tests only). Here's where things stand.\n\n**Compiled features:** your question has a clean answer. Invariant 6 means the shipped crates have no Cargo features. The only one is the dev-only `test-util`, and I confirmed it never reaches the `callisto-cli` build. #369 adds `just features-boundary` to CI so it can't later.\n\n**Open PRs:**\n\n| PR | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| #368 | Fix: installs the workflow linters in the release workflow's verify job (no release PR has been created since) |\n| #369 | CI now runs `machete` and the shipped-features guard on every PR, `semver-checks` on the release PR, and blocks on per-crate coverage at 90%. It removes two unused dependencies and adds tests for the manifest crate's publish rules and error states |\n| #370 | Docs, stacked on #369: README quick start, CONTRIBUTING setup/recipes/checklist, architecture notes on the cost rules. It drops the hand-kept \"N error codes\" line that conflicted on every PR adding a code |\n| #372 | Cascade tests: a property test over random dependency graphs plus the grammar-mismatch, catalog, opaque and stale-group-member cases |\n\n**Decision for you:** `callisto-model` is the MIT library others can depend on, and about 955 of its public items have no docs. I did not start on it. Do you want me to add `#![warn(missing_docs)]` and document the wire-contract types first (`ReleaseIntentV1`, the report types), or leave library docs until after v1?\n\n**Next:** capability/staleness tests and the CLI `release` execute path, then `callisto-manifests` edge cases for hand-formatted manifests. After that, the weekly mutation and fuzz jobs.\n\nresult: PRs #368, #369, #370 and #372 opened (release unblock, CI gates, docs refresh, cascade property tests), each with full local CI passing, and the shipped-features question is answered."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":908,"cache_read_input_tokens":508614,"output_tokens":678,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":908,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":678,"cache_read_input_tokens":508614,"cache_creation_input_tokens":908,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":908},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d6441010-fafc-4e4f-a861-55817edde3ff","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPJEqW42VeGLciT4p3As","requestRef":"c10d6afd-52af-4d87-81c7-17146d02d285","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0599617a-9a7f-4204-b326-9c1aefc76ede","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:49:08.065Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"test/cascade-properties","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
